{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.slack_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.slack_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L102-L110","doc":"**The slack above any fixed link is unbounded.** For every link and every\n`N` there is a mass number at which the crossing bound exceeds that link's\ncrossing number by at least `N` — the fit gets freer as `A` grows, not tighter.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.not_selective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.not_selective","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L89-L100","doc":"**The bound is never selective.** At every `A ≥ 1` there are two links with\ndifferent crossing numbers that are both admissible, so no `A` singles one out.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.admissible_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.admissible_mono","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L82-L87","doc":"**Admissibility only grows.** A link admissible at `A` stays admissible at\nevery larger mass number, so the substrate bound never removes a candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.braidIndexBound_lt_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.braidIndexBound_lt_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L76-L80","doc":"The braid-index bound is strictly increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.crossingBound_lt_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.crossingBound_lt_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L69-L74","doc":"The crossing bound is strictly increasing once `A ≥ 1` (below that the\ntruncated subtraction flattens it, and no nucleus has `A = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.admissible_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.admissible_iff","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L64-L67","doc":"Admissibility spelled out as plain arithmetic, so `omega` can be handed the\ngoal directly rather than being asked to see through a projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.Admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.Admissible","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L60-L62","doc":"A link is admissible at `A` when it satisfies both substrate bounds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.instDecidableEqLinkData.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.instDecidableEqLinkData.decEq","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.instDecidableEqLinkData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.instDecidableEqLinkData","kind":"instance","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.braidIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.braidIndex","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.crossings","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.LinkData","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The data a complexity bound can see about a link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.braidIndexBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.braidIndexBound","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L49-L52","doc":"Braid-index bound the substrate supplies at mass number `A`: the atom\noccupies three strands per nucleon, so its closure has braid index at most\n`3 * A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.crossingBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SubstrateComplexityBound.crossingBound","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SubstrateComplexityBoundMonotone.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Crossing bound the substrate supplies at mass number `A`: the number of\ngenuine braid letters in the canonical atom word, measured as `10 * A - 2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}